From: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 14:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] mtd: spinand: esmt: match F50D2G41KA with QPIC ID length

The ESMT F50D2G41KA returns the four-byte ID `c8 51 7f 7f` through
Qualcomm QPIC. The generic entry currently requires a fifth byte and
therefore fails to match on QPIC. Detection then falls through to the
GigaDevice entry for the same `c8:51` prefix, which describes a 128 MiB
part and truncates the 256 MiB device.

Keep matching the ESMT entry by the complete ID available from QPIC: the
manufacturer byte plus the three returned device bytes. This is a table
entry correction and does not relax matching for other SPI NAND parts.

Signed-off-by: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>

--- a/drivers/mtd/nand/spi/esmt.c
+++ b/drivers/mtd/nand/spi/esmt.c
@@ -225,7 +225,7 @@ static const struct spinand_info esmt_c8
 		     SPINAND_FACT_OTP_INFO(2, 0, &f50l1g41lb_fact_otp_ops)),
 	SPINAND_INFO("F50D2G41KA",
 		     SPINAND_ID(SPINAND_READID_METHOD_OPCODE_ADDR, 0x51, 0x7f,
-				0x7f, 0x7f),
+				0x7f),
 		     NAND_MEMORG(1, 2048, 128, 64, 2048, 40, 1, 1, 1),
 		     NAND_ECCREQ(8, 512),
 		     SPINAND_INFO_OP_VARIANTS(&read_cache_variants,
